      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nettuno’s harbor hosts about 860 boats and a bustling shopping centre for fishing and sailing gear.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nettuno",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town celebrates the Cacchione di Nettuno DOP, a white wine from Bellone grapes, during its annual Wine Festival each September.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlazio.com/en/nettuno/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Nettuno was the site of the 1944 Allied landing that sparked the Battle of Anzio during World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nettuno",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The medieval Borgo Medievale, once a fortified center, now forms the historic core of Nettuno.",
